  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for Country Partnership for Burkina Faso (2026-2030)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Burkina Faso has articulated its strategic vision for economic and social transformation through the Plan National de D&#xe9;veloppement (PND) 2026#2030, which builds on the achievements of the PNDES 2021#2025 and the country#s broader Vision prospective Burkina 2060. This plan serves as the overarching framework for public policies and investment priorities across all sectors, outlining the pathway toward a sovereign, prosperous, inclusive, and resilient economy by 2030. As such, it represents the primary reference document for all national and international development partners in aligning their cooperation frameworks with Burkina Faso#s national priorities.  Burkina Faso has demonstrated a clear and formal commitment to strengthening its strategic cooperation with UNIDO through the Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) framework. This commitment was concretized by the Prime Minister#s official request addressed to the UNIDO Director General on 25 August 2025, expressing the Government#s strong interest in establishing a comprehensive and integrated partnership to support the implementation of the National Development Plan (PND) 2026#2030 named #RELANCE#. The Government has further indicated its readiness to assume leadership in coordination, partnership-building, and resource mobilization for</narrative>
  </description>
